1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Last time on Zombieland Saga, we ran out of money even though we haven't really done anything yet.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Which is why we decided to accept our first offer for a paid appearance.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
And it was at a hot spring!

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
We even got to take in the sights around town and have some fun!

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The show was awesome, and we snuck into the bath even though we weren't supposed to.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
A girl's gotta celebrate, right?

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Let's just say we weren't very discreet, and our chance at a partnership was dead on arrival.

8
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Partially my fault, I guess.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Sorry, guys!

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Time to play ball!

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
It's the championship game to determine the Ultimate Idol team!

12
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
We're now in the ninth inning with three runs apiece!

13
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Will Team Franshu-shu be able to hold it together against the competitor?

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Here comes their race pitcher, Saki Nekaito!

15
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Huh?

16
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Just kidding, I'm gonna pitch instead!

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Oh yeah!

18
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
HOME RUN!

19
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
DARE YOU TO TRY THAT AGAIN, PRICK!

20
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,000
There!

21
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Um, sir?

22
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
What are you doing on the floor?

23
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Sweeping up my dignity!

24
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The old diamond is a cruel mistress!

25
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
You let your guard down for a second, you strike out!

26
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Oh, okay.

27
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:21,000
The point is, you better not slack off, or you'll be in real trouble, you undead stupid heads!

28
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Did you forget your little mishap?

29
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
You spilled da brains!

30
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Uh...

31
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Right.

32
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
We want idle buzz, not zombie buzz!

33
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Thanks to you, our budget's been disemboweled!

34
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,000
You're the one spending money, so...

35
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Say what you want, but your illustrious manager has secured a gig for you that's such an easy home run, even you slobs can't blow it!

36
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:47,000
We need to start boosting our profile, so the logical thing to do is appear in a commercial spot for an extremely well-known and successful business here in Saga.

37
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Wow, you mean we're getting offers for commercials now?

38
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,000
That's how I do, babe.

39
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
And when you hear who it is, it might just shock you back to life!

40
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Are you ready?

41
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
The business in question is none other than...

42
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The Famous Drive-In Toriii!

43
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
I lower the complaint blame?

44
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Where are you working!

45
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Fizze...

46
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
What's the name?

47
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
You

48
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:46,746
Holy crap. It really is driving, Toddy.

49
00:03:47,126 --> 00:03:47,946
Driving who?

50
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:48,886
You don't know?

51
00:03:49,126 --> 00:03:51,546
Respect the gods of chicken or you're undead meat.

52
00:03:51,746 --> 00:03:52,726
I'm sorry, okay.

53
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:55,186
I've heard of it, but I've never been.

54
00:03:55,906 --> 00:03:56,866
What the hell?

55
00:03:56,866 --> 00:03:59,606
All you punks fail at Saga!

56
00:04:01,086 --> 00:04:02,626
Is it that great?

57
00:04:02,786 --> 00:04:04,266
Well, you can form your own opinion.

58
00:04:04,266 --> 00:04:06,206
We'll be shooting it very soon.

59
00:04:06,406 --> 00:04:07,826
Really? When do we start?

60
00:04:07,986 --> 00:04:08,906
We start right now!

61
00:04:15,966 --> 00:04:19,066
Well, it definitely has a mom and pop feel, doesn't it?

62
00:04:19,166 --> 00:04:20,746
This is the famous place?

63
00:04:21,146 --> 00:04:23,086
It's just like coming home again.

64
00:04:23,326 --> 00:04:24,446
Sure takes me back.

65
00:04:24,446 --> 00:04:35,466
When I was alive, me and my girls used to spend all day and night raising hell.

66
00:04:35,726 --> 00:04:38,886
And afterwards, we'd hit drive-in Toddy for late night eats.

67
00:04:39,466 --> 00:04:44,626
I remember the number one yakitori meal was our go-to for the big side of lettuce.

68
00:04:44,626 --> 00:04:49,626
You had a pretty wild lifestyle, huh, Saki?

69
00:04:49,966 --> 00:04:51,746
That chicken's kind of grody.

70
00:04:51,826 --> 00:04:55,106
Your face is going to be grody if you keep talking crap about Coco!

71
00:04:55,786 --> 00:04:56,566
Coco, huh?

72
00:04:57,246 --> 00:04:58,226
What's the holdup?

73
00:04:58,346 --> 00:04:59,786
Look alive, deadbeats!

74
00:04:59,946 --> 00:05:02,306
Say hello to the esteemed president of Drive-in Toddy.

75
00:05:03,306 --> 00:05:05,186
It's nice to make your acquaintance.

76
00:05:05,446 --> 00:05:06,186
Hello, Sam.

77
00:05:06,246 --> 00:05:07,366
This is a huge honor!

78
00:05:08,366 --> 00:05:09,206
Jeez, weirdo.

79
00:05:09,206 --> 00:05:11,106
I appreciate you coming today.

80
00:05:11,426 --> 00:05:15,406
I'm really looking forward to seeing what you bring to the table for our advertising campaign.

81
00:05:15,726 --> 00:05:18,546
Let's go in so you can sample our signature grilled chicken.

82
00:05:19,326 --> 00:05:20,626
That sounds great!

83
00:05:20,766 --> 00:05:21,506
I'm not worthy!

84
00:05:31,806 --> 00:05:35,406
Most people tend to think of beef when it comes to yakiniku-style grilling,

85
00:05:35,406 --> 00:05:38,126
but in Saga Prefecture, it's all about chicken.

86
00:05:38,126 --> 00:05:43,246
Hey, Sakura, try some of that sauce with the garlic pepper.

87
00:05:44,566 --> 00:05:46,166
Ooh, this is a good piece.

88
00:05:46,526 --> 00:05:46,966
Hey!

89
00:05:47,286 --> 00:05:49,646
I was poking that for me, big baby!

90
00:05:50,006 --> 00:05:51,346
You should take that one, Ralee.

91
00:05:51,406 --> 00:05:52,206
It's already well done.

92
00:05:53,666 --> 00:05:55,806
What are you looking at there, Lady Shunko?

93
00:05:56,186 --> 00:05:58,666
Says they have a honey and black vinegar cactus.

94
00:05:59,146 --> 00:05:59,946
Bet that's good.

95
00:06:00,006 --> 00:06:00,226
What?

96
00:06:00,346 --> 00:06:02,966
Those are the seven basic principles of our company.

97
00:06:03,266 --> 00:06:03,546
Oh.

98
00:06:03,926 --> 00:06:05,846
Hey, would it kill you to listen up?

99
00:06:05,846 --> 00:06:07,946
It's all right, really.

100
00:06:08,066 --> 00:06:10,946
I'm just happy to see that they're enjoying the food so much.

101
00:06:11,646 --> 00:06:13,466
Yeah, it really is incredible.

102
00:06:13,866 --> 00:06:14,386
Thank you.

103
00:06:14,446 --> 00:06:15,226
That's great to hear.

104
00:06:15,306 --> 00:06:17,066
All the chicken we serve is fresh and...

105
00:06:17,066 --> 00:06:17,646
I know!

106
00:06:17,746 --> 00:06:19,266
It's not safe to eat it wrong!

107
00:06:19,266 --> 00:06:19,526
Oh!

108
00:06:20,526 --> 00:06:24,906
Hey, I said it's fresh, but not that fresh!

109
00:06:24,906 --> 00:06:30,366
Now then, let's talk about what you want from that chute.

110
00:06:37,966 --> 00:06:38,486
Woo-hoo!

111
00:06:39,386 --> 00:06:42,606
The one time we don't have to wear t-shirts and they put us in these.

112
00:06:43,066 --> 00:06:44,926
But this will help pay for better outfits.

113
00:06:45,606 --> 00:06:47,546
That looks so great on you, Junko!

114
00:06:48,046 --> 00:06:48,926
Don't lie to me.

115
00:06:49,126 --> 00:06:50,166
You look adorable!

116
00:06:50,166 --> 00:06:53,266
This would have been perfect in my previous line of work.

117
00:06:53,526 --> 00:06:56,566
All right, everybody, it's time to get this show on the road!

118
00:06:56,826 --> 00:07:00,306
First off, I'd like to introduce you to our lovely new singers for our commercial,

119
00:07:00,686 --> 00:07:01,846
from Shushu!

120
00:07:03,926 --> 00:07:06,386
Of course, we also have our beloved mascot,

121
00:07:06,906 --> 00:07:07,946
Give It Up for Coco!

122
00:07:07,946 --> 00:07:08,086
Coco!

123
00:07:08,086 --> 00:07:08,446
Coco!

124
00:07:08,446 --> 00:07:22,226
We're in the presence of true greatness!

125
00:07:22,606 --> 00:07:23,406
Just breathe!

126
00:07:23,866 --> 00:07:25,066
Yeah, you're getting creepy.

127
00:07:34,366 --> 00:07:36,406
Um, sorry, sir!

128
00:07:36,406 --> 00:07:38,606
Back off!

129
00:07:38,766 --> 00:07:39,846
You can't eat Coco!

130
00:07:40,086 --> 00:07:42,586
They told me not to say this, but that's just a guy in a suit!

131
00:07:42,826 --> 00:07:43,826
Hmm, hmm, hmm, hmm!

132
00:07:43,906 --> 00:07:47,646
Now, if everybody's ready, I say we go ahead and work through the first take!

133
00:07:47,786 --> 00:07:48,406
Let's rock!

134
00:07:48,726 --> 00:07:50,046
Thanks for having us!

135
00:07:50,266 --> 00:07:52,026
And we won't let you down!

136
00:07:52,186 --> 00:07:53,426
This'll be a dry run!

137
00:07:53,626 --> 00:07:54,446
And action!

138
00:07:54,446 --> 00:07:54,546
Action!

139
00:07:57,246 --> 00:07:59,446
Try the yuck and tori plate, or a chicken rice bowl,

140
00:07:59,526 --> 00:08:01,286
Healthy and delicious salads, too!

141
00:08:01,686 --> 00:08:03,286
Great service with a smile!

142
00:08:03,626 --> 00:08:05,266
Stop by and stay a while!

143
00:08:05,446 --> 00:08:05,766
Yay!

144
00:08:05,766 --> 00:08:06,386
Cut!

145
00:08:07,146 --> 00:08:07,586
Cut!

146
00:08:08,526 --> 00:08:11,306
Uh, is there something wrong with the vocals?

147
00:08:11,626 --> 00:08:12,166
Mm-hmm.

148
00:08:12,726 --> 00:08:13,726
We'll fix it.

149
00:08:14,146 --> 00:08:15,106
Sing better!

150
00:08:15,506 --> 00:08:16,506
Saki, stop.

151
00:08:16,686 --> 00:08:17,986
You know she can't do it.

152
00:08:18,406 --> 00:08:19,666
What should we do?

153
00:08:19,946 --> 00:08:20,526
You ready?

154
00:08:21,326 --> 00:08:22,666
Well, I'm not sure.

155
00:08:22,846 --> 00:08:25,826
Just cut out all of that demonic growling, and it'll be perfect.

156
00:08:25,966 --> 00:08:26,346
Rolling!

157
00:08:26,886 --> 00:08:27,986
Wait, we're not!

158
00:08:28,106 --> 00:08:29,146
We're all set, guys!

159
00:08:29,886 --> 00:08:31,286
Okay, here's the plan.

160
00:08:31,286 --> 00:08:33,426
You just do the cock-a-doodle-doo at the end, Ty.

161
00:08:33,906 --> 00:08:34,306
Ugh.

162
00:08:34,966 --> 00:08:36,246
This one's for real.

163
00:08:36,446 --> 00:08:36,826
Second take!

164
00:08:37,746 --> 00:08:37,966
Yeah!

165
00:08:38,146 --> 00:08:38,486
Ready?

166
00:08:38,986 --> 00:08:39,546
Go!

167
00:08:39,546 --> 00:08:39,826
Yeah!

168
00:08:43,826 --> 00:08:44,146
Cut!

169
00:08:44,386 --> 00:08:45,006
Yeah, cut!

170
00:08:45,346 --> 00:08:46,046
I'm sorry!

171
00:08:46,046 --> 00:09:14,626
Let's do a quick check and move on.

172
00:09:14,626 --> 00:09:18,546
It was a great idea to change the harmony at the end.

173
00:09:18,546 --> 00:09:21,286
That works.

174
00:09:21,506 --> 00:09:23,666
He is downright obsessed with it!

175
00:09:24,866 --> 00:09:26,186
That's such a relief.

176
00:09:26,366 --> 00:09:27,846
I'm not sure I agree.

177
00:09:28,806 --> 00:09:30,846
You really think you nailed that?

178
00:09:30,986 --> 00:09:31,546
Um...

179
00:09:32,206 --> 00:09:33,206
Look at yourselves.

180
00:09:33,466 --> 00:09:35,686
What exactly are you girls supposed to be?

181
00:09:36,186 --> 00:09:37,186
Idols, I think.

182
00:09:37,266 --> 00:09:37,906
You're chickens!

183
00:09:38,566 --> 00:09:39,926
This place serves chicken!

184
00:09:40,626 --> 00:09:42,066
Am I right or wrong?

185
00:09:42,446 --> 00:09:43,166
You're right!

186
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:45,846
You have to be so much more chicken-y!

187
00:09:46,746 --> 00:09:49,146
Crank that squawking chicken energy up to 11!

188
00:09:49,566 --> 00:09:52,986
I need to be able to picture you sizzling on top of a tabletop grill!

189
00:09:53,326 --> 00:09:54,286
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

190
00:09:54,366 --> 00:09:55,486
Your job!

191
00:09:55,486 --> 00:09:58,706
For once, I think I might agree with him.

192
00:09:58,706 --> 00:09:59,006
Huh?

193
00:10:00,366 --> 00:10:02,446
Guys, we failed.

194
00:10:03,226 --> 00:10:05,806
They wanted real chickens and we blew it!

195
00:10:07,166 --> 00:10:09,206
But that tape was okay.

196
00:10:09,426 --> 00:10:12,326
I know you're stupid, but I promise you they can do this!

197
00:10:12,546 --> 00:10:14,066
Please, just one more chance!

198
00:10:14,406 --> 00:10:15,666
I mean, look!

199
00:10:16,326 --> 00:10:18,886
Come on, you don't want to let Coco show us up, do you?

200
00:10:18,886 --> 00:10:25,606
If we're going to take over all of Japan, we've got to be able to gobble up the star of the whole show!

201
00:10:27,626 --> 00:10:28,466
I know!

202
00:10:38,466 --> 00:10:40,346
Somebody stop her!

203
00:10:40,446 --> 00:10:40,826
Hurry!

204
00:10:40,926 --> 00:10:41,446
Yes, sir!

205
00:10:41,866 --> 00:10:42,626
Wait!

206
00:10:44,706 --> 00:10:46,006
Roll that camera!

207
00:10:46,406 --> 00:10:47,406
This is reality!

208
00:10:48,886 --> 00:10:51,906
This is the story we never knew we needed to see!

209
00:10:52,526 --> 00:10:52,846
Stop!

210
00:10:53,046 --> 00:10:53,626
She didn't see!

211
00:10:53,706 --> 00:10:55,286
We should literally be chickens!

212
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,446
Say the word!

213
00:10:59,886 --> 00:11:00,446
Action!

214
00:11:01,446 --> 00:11:01,726
Oh!

215
00:11:06,406 --> 00:11:08,086
Great job with the commercial.

216
00:11:08,546 --> 00:11:09,786
You were so into it.

217
00:11:10,006 --> 00:11:11,866
This is our way of showing our gratitude.

218
00:11:13,126 --> 00:11:14,426
You think it's food?

219
00:11:16,106 --> 00:11:17,126
T-shirts.

220
00:11:17,126 --> 00:11:19,926
More T-shirts.

221
00:11:20,306 --> 00:11:22,366
I'm excited to see the final product.

222
00:11:23,406 --> 00:11:23,906
Hmm?

223
00:11:25,706 --> 00:11:26,266
Hmm.

224
00:11:26,266 --> 00:11:38,206
Hey, that's a new ad.

225
00:11:39,646 --> 00:11:40,906
Local idols, huh?

226
00:11:41,766 --> 00:11:43,426
Must be hard to do that in Saga.

227
00:11:44,806 --> 00:11:46,546
Have I seen that girl before?

228
00:11:48,766 --> 00:11:50,066
Good job, girls!

229
00:11:50,066 --> 00:11:52,006
You make some nice birds!

230
00:11:52,006 --> 00:11:53,526
Real nice birds!

231
00:11:53,546 --> 00:11:54,046
I serve you, but it's a new diet.

232
00:11:54,046 --> 00:12:03,286
T-shirts!

233
00:12:03,286 --> 00:12:08,026
I still need to recognize it, too!

234
00:12:10,806 --> 00:12:12,146
Thank you.

235
00:12:12,146 --> 00:12:12,646
Si.

236
00:12:15,386 --> 00:12:18,046
Bonjour, Saga Jeune.

237
00:12:18,486 --> 00:12:18,906
What?

238
00:12:19,506 --> 00:12:20,806
Cause you're in Saga.

239
00:12:21,326 --> 00:12:23,886
Yeah, I guess I am a Saga Jeune now.

240
00:12:24,506 --> 00:12:26,546
What makes you a Saga Jeune?

241
00:12:30,086 --> 00:12:31,346
What's with you?

242
00:12:31,846 --> 00:12:32,766
There he goes.

243
00:12:34,766 --> 00:12:35,686
Listen up!

244
00:12:35,886 --> 00:12:37,006
The way you are right now,

245
00:12:37,106 --> 00:12:38,966
not one of you snot-wiping loser zombies

246
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,606
gets to call yourself a Saga Jeune.

247
00:12:40,606 --> 00:12:42,946
But I've come up with a way

248
00:12:42,946 --> 00:12:44,226
to turn you into Saga Jeunes

249
00:12:44,226 --> 00:12:46,686
who could rival the fair Mademoiselle Zeperri.

250
00:12:47,366 --> 00:12:49,726
Time for the Gat-Olympics!

251
00:12:50,426 --> 00:12:51,226
No way, man.

252
00:12:52,366 --> 00:12:54,026
We get to compete?

253
00:12:54,346 --> 00:12:55,306
Crying again?

254
00:12:55,546 --> 00:12:57,646
You do know anyone can enter that, right?

255
00:12:57,806 --> 00:12:59,126
What even is it, though?

256
00:12:59,666 --> 00:13:00,846
You don't know?

257
00:13:01,126 --> 00:13:03,246
All of you fail at Saga-

258
00:13:05,246 --> 00:13:07,046
Ew, gross.

259
00:13:07,366 --> 00:13:09,266
It's not very glamorous, is it?

260
00:13:09,266 --> 00:13:10,766
Yeah, I don't wanna.

261
00:13:11,306 --> 00:13:12,186
Too bad!

262
00:13:14,606 --> 00:13:17,426
That is the ugliest freaking shirt I've ever seen.

263
00:13:17,606 --> 00:13:18,306
Like it or not,

264
00:13:18,386 --> 00:13:20,206
you ladies will each be sporting one of these

265
00:13:20,206 --> 00:13:21,926
while you're competing in the Gat-Olympics.

266
00:13:22,066 --> 00:13:22,726
Sounds good.

267
00:13:22,806 --> 00:13:23,466
When is it, though?

268
00:13:23,466 --> 00:13:24,606
It's right now!

269
00:13:24,606 --> 00:13:37,266
This kind of reminds me of those swimsuit-only sporting events

270
00:13:37,266 --> 00:13:38,046
they used to have.

